{"title":"Abbreviating The Product Of A Range","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"Given integers `left` and `right`, calculate the product of all integers in the inclusive range `[left, right]` and return its abbreviated form.\n\nRemove every trailing zero from the product and let `C` be the number removed. Let `d` be the number of digits remaining. If `d <= 10`, keep all remaining digits. If `d > 10`, use the first five digits, followed by `...`, followed by the last five digits. Preserve any leading zeros within those last five digits.\n\nAppend `eC` to this representation. For example, `12345678987600000` becomes `\"12345...89876e5\"`.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: left = 1, right = 4\nOutput: \"24e0\"\n```\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: left = 2, right = 11\nOutput: \"399168e2\"\n```\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: left = 371, right = 375\nOutput: \"7219856259e3\"\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 <= left <= right <= 10^4\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def abbreviateProduct(self, left: int, right: int) -> str:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().abbreviateProduct","parameters":[{"name":"left","type":"int"},{"name":"right","type":"int"}],"returnType":"str","tests":[{"input":[1,1],"expected":"1e0"},{"input":[1,10000],"expected":"28462...79008e2499"},{"input":[1,30],"expected":"26525...30848e7"},{"input":[1,4],"expected":"24e0"},{"input":[10000,10000],"expected":"1e4"},{"input":[1001,1129],"expected":"31175...87008e31"},{"input":[1001,1174],"expected":"18110...14368e41"},{"input":[1005,1011],"expected":"10573...33232e2"},{"input":[1021,1062],"expected":"55011...58528e10"},{"input":[1021,1161],"expected":"19526...49376e35"},{"input":[1023,1111],"expected":"31291...00384e22"},{"input":[1031,1056],"expected":"30235...19008e6"},{"input":[1032,1080],"expected":"14375...68416e12"},{"input":[1044,1153],"expected":"29378...37984e28"},{"input":[1047,1226],"expected":"83299...87008e45"},{"input":[106,243],"expected":"53311...48672e33"},{